# aws — core AWS concepts

## Elastic Load Balancing

A Layer 4 load balancer works at the network protocol level without looking inside packets, unaware of HTTP/HTTPS specifics. A Layer 7 load balancer inspects packets, sees HTTP/HTTPS headers, and can spread load more intelligently.

| Type | Layer | Notes                                                        |
| ---- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| ELB  | 4     | classic                                                      |
| ALB  | 7     | content-based routing (up to 10 URL rules), container-aware port-level health checks |
| NLB  | 4     | much larger traffic volume; spans geographically distinct subnets |

## Data storage types

| Service               | Behaves like                | Key trait                        |
| --------------------- | --------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| Instance store volume | local disk                  | disappears with the instance     |
| EBS                   | physical NAS drive          | tied to a single instance        |
| EFS                   | NFS                         | distributed, multi-instance      |
| S3                    | NAS, not tied to instances  | object storage                   |
| Glacier               | cold storage                | slow retrieval, cheap            |

## Database services

| Service    | Notes                                        |
| ---------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| RDS        | MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, MSSQL             |
| RDS Aurora | MySQL compatible — HA and performance scaling |
| DynamoDB   | NoSQL                                        |

## Locations

Regions (e.g. us-west-1 California, us-west-2 Oregon) contain a minimum of 3 availability zones (datacenters): `us-west-1a,b,c`.

## Accounts and security

VPC accounts define one or more virtual private clouds, each with its own private network and IP range. Security groups define rules controlling access to member resources — a firewall around the group; a resource in multiple groups gets the aggregate of the rules.

## Monitoring

| Service    | Purpose                                                     |
| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| CloudWatch | resource metrics, costs, drives auto scaling                |
| CloudTrail | logs management API calls and console actions (audit trail) |

## Real-world: check what a mystery EC2 bill is running

```sh
aws ec2 describe-instances \
  --query 'Reservations[].Instances[].[InstanceId,InstanceType,State.Name]' \
  --output table
```

See the `awscli` sheet for command-line usage.
